{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And I shall lie with my fathers.</b> With reference to the soul. <b>And you shall carry me out of Egypt</b> — with reference to the body. That is: I am assured that even if you bury me in Egypt, I go to my fathers; only you would cause me a rolling-about (gilgul). Rabbi Yitsḥak said: from here we learn that a person knows on the day of his death where he is going — whether to the place of the righteous or to the place of the wicked. And this is why he put first 'and I shall lie with my fathers' and afterward 'and you shall carry me out of Egypt' — meaning, even if a person dies in a wagon, or on a ship, or in a river, or in the wilderness, or in a settled place, his soul goes first and journeys to his fathers. And we find of R. Abbahu that he saw the granting of his reward close to his death, for so they expounded in Elleh HaDevarim Rabbah in the parashah of 'Vehayah Ekev' (Psalms 31:20): ״מה רב טובך אשר צפנת ליראיך״. There was an incident involving R. Abbahu, who was dying, and he saw the granting of his reward — that which the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to give him in the world to come, and all the good prepared for the righteous. And when he saw all those prepared consolations, he said: 'All these for Abbahu?' Immediately he longed for death. He began to recite: ״מה רב טובך אשר צפנת ליראיך״." "<b>And you shall bury me in their burial.</b> From here the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: a person should always bury a righteous person next to righteous people, as it is said (II Kings 13:21): ״ויהי הם קוברים איש והנה ראו את הגדוד״, etc. And this is what the prophet said at his death (I Kings 13:31): ״וקברתם אותי בקבר אשר איש האלהים קבור בו אצל עצמותיו הניחו עצמותי״." "<b>I will do as you have spoken.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he acknowledged him in the matter. <b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'I will do as you have spoken' — just as you had me swear, so I will make the tribes swear that they shall bring me up."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:05.138031025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}